- Overlay chrome: put title/tags in a **row below** the player (`BrdGalleryOverlayInfo` on Library). Toggle that bar with **Details** (`BtnGalleryDetails`, icon + text, Ctrl+I, `ShowDetails`; default on, then LocalSettings `GalleryShowDetails`) — do not cover `MediaPlayer` transport. Animated GIF stills keep autoplay via `GifFrames` delays + composite frames (`GifPlaying`); Pause keeps `GifFrameIndex` instead of restarting `BitmapImage`. `GalleryStillSurface` loads frames once with `TryRenderAll` and applies ticks from that cache — play `GifFrameIndex` ticks must not `RefreshAsync` / cancel that load while the cache is empty (`ShouldApplyGifTick` / `ShouldStartGifCompositeLoad`). The delay clock waits until composites exist (`ShouldRunGifPlayLoop` / `NotifyGifCompositeReady`) so Pause/slider during load keep frame 0. Library and Tags `CloseOverlay` plus `GalleryWindow` Closed call `StopGifPlayback`; `Bind(null)` also stops that clock so a late `NotifyGifCompositeReady` cannot keep the VM alive after Esc/close. Applying a cached GIF cancels a stale other-path `_gifLoadCts` (`ShouldCancelStaleGifLoad`). `TryRenderAll` honors the load cancel token. `FitsCacheBudget` is overflow-safe (divide, not `width*height*4*frames` which wraps) and caps 256 MB / 2048 frames. `FitsFramePixels` caps image-descriptor `fw*fh` the same way so `DecodeLzw` / `Blit` cannot allocate ~2 GB off a small logical screen — oversized GIFs skip scrub (`gifInfo` null) and stay on the non-scrub still path with `ToStillImage(..., animateGif: true)` so `BitmapImage` still autoplays. Failed `TryRenderAll` after scrub was offered abandons chrome (`AbandonGifScrub` / `ShouldAbandonScrubOnFailedComposite`) and falls back to `ToStillImage(..., animateGif: true)`. Scrub `ToStillImage` keeps `AutoPlay` off. Switching onto a GIF still bumps the HDR `_epoch` (`ShouldBumpHdrEpochOnGifStillRefresh`) so a late WIC/scRGB present cannot replace `ImgStill`, without cancelling `TryRenderAll`. Overlay (`BrdGifScrub` / `BtnGifPlay` / `BtnGifPause` / `BtnGifPrevFrame` / `SldGifFrame` / `BtnGifNextFrame` / `TxtGifFrame`) and `GalleryWindow` (`BrdGalleryWindowGifScrub` / `BtnGalleryWindowGifPlay` / `BtnGalleryWindowGifPause` / `BtnGalleryWindowGifPrevFrame` / `SldGalleryWindowGifFrame` / `BtnGalleryWindowGifNextFrame` / `TxtGalleryWindowGifFrame`) add Pause / Play / prev-next frame / timeline on **local hydrated** `.gif` only (`GifFrames.CanScrub`, two or more frames) — do not recall On-Demand to scrub, and do not put GIF chrome over `MediaPlayer` transport. Overlay / GalleryWindow PreviewKeyDown must not mark Left/Right handled while `SldGifFrame` / `SldGalleryWindowGifFrame` is focused (`PassesGifSliderArrows`) — the slider nudges the frame; Left/Right elsewhere still change the asset. `GalleryWindow` details are a **right column** (`BrdGalleryWindowDetails` / `ScrGalleryWindowDetails`) with the same `ShowDetails` toggle (`BtnGalleryWindowDetails`); long prompt/description scrolls in that column, not a bottom Auto row. The overlay bar is compact and opaque (`SolidBackgroundFillColorSecondaryBrush`) — not a full-width `LayerFill` card and not over `MediaPlayer` transport (settings / seek). Tall generation / prompt / negative text scrolls inside `ScrPrompt` / `ScrOverlayPrompt` / `ScrGalleryWindowPrompt` (`MaxHeight`); do not grow the overlay or details column forever. Overlay / `GalleryWindow` stills use **1:1 / Fit / Fill** (`GalleryScale`, Ctrl+1/2/3, icon + text). **1:1** is one device pixel per oriented image pixel (`ActualDipSize` = pixels / raster scale). Size the Image to those DIPs and use `Stretch.Uniform` — `Stretch.None` paints PixelWidth DIPs and clips at >100% DPI. Not catalog Width/Height (unoriented). **Fill** covers the viewport (crop overflow), **centers** the cover crop (`CoverCenterOffset` / `InitialScrollOffset`), and pans the overflow. Recenter/reset pinch and scroll when the still, scale, or viewport size changes so a prior pan does not stick. 1:1 and Fill pan with **left-click drag** (`GalleryScale.UsesPointerCapturePan`) and **touch/pen** ManipulationDelta (`DragPan`); pinch scale is `GalleryScale.PinchZoom` (1–8) on `GalleryStillSurface` (Fit letterboxes until pinch). A pinch frame uses one `ChangeView` via `PinchThenDrag` — do not DragPan from stale `HorizontalOffset` after pinch. Pen stays off pointer-capture pan so it does not pan twice. Details and an HDR line come from `GalleryPresent` + `HdrFile` / `AvifFile` (header-only; skip online-only). Magick TGA/EXR stay out. Radiance `.hdr` is isolated C# RGBE (`RadianceFile`); PSD / HEIC / JXR / JXL / DDS are catalog stills without Magick. Catalog stills include `.avif` `.heic` `.heif` `.jxr` `.wdp` `.hdp` `.jxl` `.hdr` `.psd` `.dds` (`PathSafe.ImageExt`). Decode is inbox WIC (HEIF/AV1/JXL Store codecs) or C# RGBE, libavif for HDR AVIF only (`Starward.Codec` `avif.dll`); HDR JPEG XR (`.jxr` / `.wdp` / `.hdp`) presents via native WIC COM float/half into that same swapchain (WinRT has no float pixel format — do not `BitmapImage` the original). Not libjxl / Magick. HDR PNG and HDR HEIF present scRGB on Open via `SwapChainPanel` (`HdrSwapchainPresenter` / `GalleryStillSurface`) through WIC. HDR AVIF presents via libavif (`HdrAvifDecode` / `Starward.Codec` `avif.dll`: `avifDecoderNextImage` → `avifImageYUVToRGB` → PQ/HLG → scRGB), matching SKIV — identity matrix 0 is GBR. Honor primary-item `colr` via `pitm`/`ipma`. WIC remains fallback only; do not treat WIC `Rgba16` luma-in-R as RGB/GBR (red tint MaxCLL scRGB 207.561 or green Y→G). Ultra HDR JPEG stays the SDR base plus a label. `BitmapImage` remains the SDR fallback and the mosaic path — do **not** also `BitmapImage` the original when HDR present is attempted (that double-decodes 4K PQ). First HDR paint decodes at the **viewport** (`PresentDecodeSize`); luminance stats after present come from that downscaled/viewport frame (promote `HdrFrame` CIE Y / MaxCLL, or `TryMeasureAsync` via `MeasureDecodeSize` — viewport or `FastPresentLongEdge`, never a native 16384— decode). Math stays CIE Y in source primaries and MaxCLL scRGB. **HDR present never rasterizes on the UI thread**: `HdrSwapchainPresenter.TryPresentAsync` keeps COM / XAML work (layout, device, DXGI probe, `ResizeBuffers`, upload, `Present`) on the UI thread and runs `HdrRasterize.Fill` (float to half, parallel rows, reused `HdrHalfBuffer`) on the thread pool; it re-checks `_epoch` / frame / presenter (`stillCurrent`) after the raster and before any swapchain call, so a stale or closed-overlay result never presents. `GalleryStillSurface` requests presents through `HdrPresentCoalescer` (one loop; first paint and scale mode are immediate, resize / peak ticks settle 75 ms and are capped at 250 ms) - do not call the presenter directly or add a synchronous present. 1:1 re-decodes native. PQ/HLG only when cICP transfer is 16/18 — cLLi/mDCv without transfer is sRGB, not PQ. **203 nits is BT.2408 paper / reference white**, not display peak — never label it “Display peak” and never clip auto present to 203 when DXGI is unknown (`EffectivePeakNits` / `ProbedDisplayLuminance` return 0; HDR rasterize then uses 10 000 nits). **SDR displays** (DXGI ColorSpace G22 sRGB, not advanced color / scRGB / HDR10) **tonemap** HDR stills: SKIV map-CLL-to-display + clip (`GalleryPresent.PresentMap` / `SdrPresentPeakNits` / `HdrColor.MapCllToDisplayScrgb`). G22 map target is always 80 nits (scRGB 1.0 composition white) — ignore EDID 80–220, dummy 270, and 203 paper white. G22 ColorSpace alone is not SDR: Windows HDR (SAM713F) often keeps G22 with dummy 270 — `IsHdrOutput` treats peak >220 as HDR clip-only scRGB (dummy 270 unknown peak → 10 000, not 203). DXGI probe failures (`TryQuery`, no adapter/output) must not throw past present or fall through to 80-nit SDR: `UnknownDisplayPresentsHdr` (PQ/HLG/HDR JXR) presents scRGB at unknown peak. Overlay Info `Display:` and `OutputDebugString` log CCD ACE / path count / DXGI cs+peak or the fail reason. SDR `PresentMap` uses sticky highest content MaxCLL (`StickyContentMaxNits` / `StickyContentMaxNitsForStill`), not the current `HdrFrame` decode size, so Fit viewport vs 1:1 native share one scale (header cLLi is a floor; Info MaxCLL stays the pixel peak). The sticky peak is **per still** — next/prev must not keep a prior MaxCLL. HDR displays keep scRGB present + Settings Peak override (`GalleryPeak`). Info **Display luminance** is DXGI `MaxFullFrameLuminance` (else `MaxLuminance`) when it looks like a real HDR peak (>220). **Max luminance / avg / min** are CIE Y in the source primaries **before** 2020→709 (`LuminanceY`); **MaxCLL (scRGB)** is max channel after the matrix / 80 — not cLLi metadata nits. **Resolution** is file pixels (`FilePixelSize`: WIC/native, then header `ImageDimensions`, then catalog) — never a 512 thumb when the file is 3840×2160. App-wide **Peak** override lives on Settings (`TglHdrPeakOverride` / `SldHdrPeakNits` / `TxtHdrPeakNits`, Fluent + text, LocalSettings via `GalleryPeak`); present uses that global clip when override is on. Do not put Peak on overlay or gallery-window chrome. Optional SKIV-style **Info** toggle at the top left (`BtnGalleryImageInfo` / `BrdGalleryImageInfo`, icon + text, Ctrl+D, `ShowImageInfo`) shows the file / size / resolution / color / luminance box (`GalleryPresent.ImageInfoText`). Default on (matches the SKIV shot), then LocalSettings `GalleryShowImageInfo` — Off sticks across overlay / GalleryWindow open and app restart (`GalleryChrome`). **Histogram** (`GalleryHistogram`) bins CIE Y (log nits) and scRGB R/G/B from the presented `HdrFrame` (viewport decode, not the 512 thumb, not Magick / a second viewer). Skip online-only and API thumbs (`ShouldBuild`). GalleryWindow **Details** shows Y / RGB (`BtnGalleryWindowHistogramLuma` / `BtnGalleryWindowHistogramRgb`, `TxtGalleryWindowHistogram`); compact luma under Info (`TxtGalleryWindowInfoHistogram`) and overlay Info (`TxtGalleryOverlayHistogram`) stays in the top-left Info card so it does not cover `MediaPlayer` transport. UIA: assert those `Txt*` ids (Canvas has a weak peer). Details and Info are independent. Do not add Save As / Export / Copy, a gamut triangle, or output-format radios. `CurrentProbe` is assigned **before** `CurrentPath` / `PreviewImageUri` / `IsImage`, then `StillRevision` is bumped once — `GalleryStillSurface` refreshes on `StillRevision`, not each field. `Bind` of the same gallery is a no-op; `Bind(null)` / Unloaded increment `_epoch` so an in-flight WIC decode cannot present onto a closed overlay. `ScpHdr` lives inside `ScrStill`; Actual/Fill size content from oriented `HdrFrame` or `BitmapImage` PixelWidth/Height after `ImageOpened`. Cache `HdrFrame` by path+probe — `SizeChanged` / `Scaling` re-present when a frame is cached (not only when `ScpHdr` is already Visible). Present uses layout DIPs (`Width` / `ScrStill`), never a Collapsed `ActualWidth` of 0; show `ScpHdr` under the SDR image, then hide the image on success. A still URI that is not `item.Path` (thumb / cloud preview) must `HideHdr` and clear the cache. WIC decode uses `OrientedPixelWidth` / `OrientedPixelHeight` with `RespectExifOrientation`. `ProbeDisplay` matches the window's monitor (`MonitorFromWindow`), not `EnumOutputs(0)`. CCD is `TryWindowsHdrEnabled(DeviceName)` only — do **not** `TryWindowsHdrEnabled(null)` after a named non-HDR (`WindowsHdrForNamedOutput` ignores any-path HDR). `CreateSwapChainForComposition` is vtable 24, `GetDesc1` is 27, and `SetColorSpace1` must be `DXGI_COLOR_SPACE_RGB_FULL_G10_NONE_P709` (1) or present fails. 8-bit unpack uses `HdrPixels` and the actual WIC format (Rgba8 is not BGRA).- Video posters use `StorageFile.GetThumbnailAsync` (shell/provider stream), not `BitmapDecoder` on the original. Overlay play uses `MediaPlayer.Play()` (`BtnGalleryPlay`). Overlay / GalleryWindow **Set thumb** (`BtnGallerySetThumb` / `BtnGalleryWindowSetThumb`) replaces the mosaic JPEG from the current seek position for playable local video only (`VideoMosaicThumb` / `VideoFrameThumb` → `MediaComposition.GetThumbnailAsync` + `ThumbnailService.CacheScaledJpegAsync`); never beside the source, never hydrate cloud originals just for a poster.
